{"description":"We're doing the most respectful thing we can think of to honour Dolly Parton: hot glueing rhinestones onto book covers until our hands cramp\nBring a book (your favourite, a thrift find, or something you never plan to read again) and we'll have the gun and bedazzler station ready.\nWe're talking full glam covers like sequins, gems, glitter, no such thing as too much. Dolly didn't build an empire on subtlety and neither will your book club copy of a novel you technically finished.\nOne coffee, matcha or tea drink from Mola Cafe and supplies to bedazzle your book is included.\n—\nNew members welcome, no experience required. Tickets are non refundable.\nWine About Books (WaB) is a Toronto book club for women, mostly in their 20s and 30s, who want reading to feel a bit more social and a lot less quiet. more on IG: @wab.bookclub 🍒","organizer":"Wine About Books"}